 my priority, not time."],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":30,"words":["ept-priority"]},{"id":"ept-b2-u02-l03-e01","lesson_id":"ept-b2-u02-l03","position":1,"type":"fill_blank","skill":"grammar","prompt_es":"Complete a frase","payload":{"type":"fill_blank","sentence":"You can borrow my car ___ you drive carefully.","translation":"Você pode usar meu carro desde que dirija com cuidado.","options":["as long as","in case","otherwise","although"]},"answer":"as long as","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"As long as + presente: a condição para que algo aconteça.","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":15,"words":["ept-as-long-as"]},{"id":"ept-b2-u02-l03-e02","lesson_id":"ept-b2-u02-l03","position":2,"type":"fill_blank","skill":"grammar","prompt_es":"Complete a frase","payload":{"type":"fill_blank","sentence":"Take an umbrella ___ it rains.","translation":"Leve um guarda-chuva caso chova.","options":["in case","as long as","otherwise","unless"]},"answer":"in case","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"In case: você faz algo antes, como precaução.","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":15,"words":["ept-in-case"]},{"id":"ept-b2-u02-l03-e03","lesson_id":"ept-b2-u02-l03","position":3,"type":"fill_blank","skill":"grammar","prompt_es":"Complete a frase","payload":{"type":"fill_blank","sentence":"Hurry up. ___, we will miss the train.","translation":"Corre. Senão, vamos perder o trem.","options":["Otherwise","Provided that","In case","As long as"]},"answer":"Otherwise","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":15,"words":["ept-otherwise"]},{"id":"ept-b2-u02-l03-e04","lesson_id":"ept-b2-u02-l03","position":4,"type":"fill_blank","skill":"grammar","prompt_es":"Complete a frase","payload":{"type":"fill_blank","sentence":"We will sign, provided that the price ___ the same.","translation":"Vamos assinar, contanto que o preço continue o mesmo.","options":["stays","will stay","stayed","would stay"]},"answer":"stays","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"Depois de provided that (como depois de if) vem o presente, mesmo falando do futuro; nada de subjuntivo como no português “contanto que continue”.","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":15,"words":["ept-provided-that"]},{"id":"ept-b2-u02-l03-e05","lesson_id":"ept-b2-u02-l03","position":5,"type":"context_choice","skill":"reading","prompt_es":"Leia e responda","payload":{"type":"context_choice","stimulus":{"kind":"reading","id":"ept.stim.b2-u2-offer","document":"email","setting":"Uma candidata responde a uma oferta de emprego.","from":"Laura Kim","to":"Mr. Patel","title":"Job offer","lines":["Dear Mr. Patel,","Thank you very much for the job offer. I am very excited about joining the team.","Before I accept, I would like to discuss one point. In my current job I work from home two days a week, and this flexibility is important to me.","I would be happy to accept a slightly lower salary, provided that I can keep those two days at home. Otherwise, I am afraid I would have to turn the offer down.","I hope we can reach an agreement. I am free to talk at any time this week.","Kind regards,","Laura Kim"]},"question":"Que condição a Laura impõe para aceitar a oferta?","options":["Continuar trabalhando dois dias por semana de casa","Um salário mais alto","Começar no mês que vem","Ter a própria equipe"]},"answer":"Continuar trabalhando dois dias por semana de casa","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"Laura escreve: “I would be happy to accept a slightly lower salary, provided that I can keep those two days at home”.","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":60,"words":[]},{"id":"ept-b2-u02-l03-e06","lesson_id":"ept-b2-u02-l03","position":6,"type":"context_choice","skill":"reading","prompt_es":"Leia e responda","payload":{"type":"context_choice","stimulus":{"kind":"reading","id":"ept.stim.b2-u2-offer","document":"email","setting":"Uma candidata responde a uma oferta de emprego.","from":"Laura Kim","to":"Mr. Patel","title":"Job offer","lines":["Dear Mr. Patel,","Thank you very much for the job offer. I am very excited about joining the team.","Before I accept, I would like to discuss one point. In my current job I work from home two days a week, and this flexibility is important to me.","I would be happy to accept a slightly lower salary, provided that I can keep those two days at home. Otherwise, I am afraid I would have to turn the offer down.","I hope we can reach an agreement. I am free to talk at any time this week.","Kind regards,","Laura Kim"]},"question":"O que acontece se a empresa não aceitar a condição dela?","options":["A Laura vai recusar a oferta","A Laura vai aceitar mesmo assim","A Laura vai pedir mais tempo","A Laura vai falar com o chefe atual"]},"answer":"A Laura vai recusar a oferta","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"Laura escreve: “Otherwise, I am afraid I would have to turn the offer down”.","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":60,"words":[]},{"id":"ept-b2-u02-l03-e07","lesson_id":"ept-b2-u02-l03","position":7,"type":"listen_choice","skill":"listening","prompt_es":"Ouça e escolha o que você ouve","payload":{"type":"listen_choice","audioText":"Send me the terms in writing, in case anything changes.","options":["Send me the terms in writing, in case anything changes.","Send me the terms in writing, as long as nothing changes.","Send me the terms by email, in case anything changes.","Send them the terms in writing, in case anything changes."]},"answer":"Send me the terms in writing, in case anything changes.","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":15,"words":["ept-in-case"]},{"id":"ept-b2-u02-l03-e08","lesson_id":"ept-b2-u02-l03","position":8,"type":"order_words","skill":"sentence_building","prompt_es":"Ordene as palavras","payload":{"type":"order_words","tokens":["I","will","help","you","as","long","as","you","help","me"],"translation":"Vou te ajudar desde que você me ajude."},"answer":"I will help you as long as you help me.","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":25,"words":["ept-as-long-as"]},{"id":"ept-b2-u02-l03-e09","lesson_id":"ept-b2-u02-l03","position":9,"type":"short_answer","skill":"sentence_building","prompt_es":"Responda em inglês","payload":{"type":"short_answer","question":"Why are you taking a jacket? (caso esfrie)","translation":"Por que você está levando uma jaqueta?"},"answer":"In case it gets cold.","accepted_answers":["In case it's cold.","I am taking it in case it gets cold.","I'm taking a jacket in case it gets cold."],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":30,"words":["ept-in-case"]},{"id":"ept-b2-u02-l03-e10","lesson_id":"ept-b2-u02-l03","position":10,"type":"translate_write","skill":"translation","prompt_es":"Traduza para o inglês","payload":{"type":"translate_write","source":"Corre. Senão, vamos perder o trem."},"answer":"Hurry up. Otherwise, we will miss the train.","accepted_answers":["Hurry up. Otherwise, we'll miss the train.","Hurry up. Otherwise we will miss the train.","Hurry up, otherwise we'll miss the train."],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":30,"words":["ept-otherwise"]},{"id":"ept-b2-u02-l04-e01","lesson_id":"ept-b2-u02-l04","position":1,"type":"match_pairs","skill":"vocabulary","prompt_es":"Una cada palavra ao seu significado","payload":{"type":"match_pairs","pairs":[{"left":"leader","right":"líder"},{"left":"delegate","right":"delegar"},{"left":"workload","right":"carga de trabalho"},{"left":"persuade","right":"convencer / persuadir"}]},"answer":"","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":30,"words":["ept-leader","ept-delegate","ept-workload","ept-persuade"]},{"id":"ept-b2-u02-l04-e02","lesson_id":"ept-b2-u02-l04","position":2,"type":"fill_blank","skill":"vocabulary","prompt_es":"Complete a frase","payload":{"type":"fill_blank","sentence":"She took ___ a new project last week.","translation":"Na semana passada ela assumiu um projeto novo.","options":["on","up","off","down"]},"answer":"on","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":15,"words":["ept-take-on"]},{"id":"ept-b2-u02-l04-e03","lesson_id":"ept-b2-u02-l04","position":3,"type":"fill_blank","skill":"grammar","prompt_es":"Complete a frase","payload":{"type":"fill_blank","sentence":"I persuaded my boss ___ me a day off.","translation":"Convenci meu chefe a me dar um dia de folga.","options":["to give","giving","give","gave"]},"answer":"to give","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"Persuade someone to + verbo.","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":15,"words":["ept-persuade"]},{"id":"ept-b2-u02-l04-e04","lesson_id":"ept-b2-u02-l04","position":4,"type":"context_choice","skill":"listening","prompt_es":"Ouça e responda","payload":{"type":"context_choice","stimulus":{"kind":"listening","id":"ept.stim.b2-u2-team","setting":"Uma líder de equipe conversa com um funcionário que está sobrecarregado.","speakers":[{"name":"Grace","voice":"a"},{"name":"Omar","voice":"b"}],"rate":1,"lines":[{"speaker":"Grace","text":"Omar, you look exhausted. Is your workload too heavy at the moment?"},{"speaker":"Omar","text":"Honestly, yes. I took on the new client last month, and I'm still doing my old projects."},{"speaker":"Grace","text":"You should have told me. A good leader needs to know these things."},{"speaker":"Omar","text":"I didn't want to turn down the client. I thought it was a good opportunity."},{"speaker":"Grace","text":"It is, but you can't do everything. Let's delegate the reports to Ben."},{"speaker":"Omar","text":"Are you sure? He is quite new."},{"speaker":"Grace","text":"That's fine. I'll help him at the beginning, in case he has questions."}]},"question":"Por que o Omar tem tanto trabalho?","options":["Assumiu um cliente novo e continua com os projetos de antes","Um colega pediu demissão","Está aprendendo um trabalho novo","A chefe passou para ele os relatórios do Ben"]},"answer":"Assumiu um cliente novo e continua com os projetos de antes","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"Omar diz: “I took on the new client last month, and I’m still doing my old projects”.","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":75,"words":[]},{"id":"ept-b2-u02-l04-e05","lesson_id":"ept-b2-u02-l04","position":5,"type":"context_choice","skill":"listening","prompt_es":"Ouça e responda","payload":{"type":"context_choice","stimulus":{"kind":"listening","id":"ept.stim.b2-u2-team","setting":"Uma líder de equipe conversa com um funcionário que está sobrecarregado.","speakers":[{"name":"Grace","voice":"a"},{"name":"Omar","voice":"b"}],"rate":1,"lines":[{"speaker":"Grace","text":"Omar, you look exhausted. Is your workload too heavy at the moment?"},{"speaker":"Omar","text":"Honestly, yes. I took on the new client last month, and I'm still doing my old projects."},{"speaker":"Grace","text":"You should have told me. A good leader needs to know these things."},{"speaker":"Omar","text":"I didn't want to turn down the client. I thought it was a good opportunity."},{"speaker":"Grace","text":"It is, but you can't do everything. Let's delegate the reports to Ben."},{"speaker":"Omar","text":"Are you sure? He is quite new."},{"speaker":"Grace","text":"That's fine. I'll help him at the beginning, in case he has questions."}]},"question":"Que solução a Grace propõe?","options":["Delegar os relatórios para o Ben e ajudá-lo no começo","Recusar o cliente novo","Contratar outra pessoa","Que o Omar trabalhe no fim de semana"]},"answer":"Delegar os relatórios para o Ben e ajudá-lo no começo","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"Grace diz: “Let’s delegate the reports to Ben… I’ll help him at the beginning”.","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":75,"words":[]},{"id":"ept-b2-u02-l04-e06","lesson_id":"ept-b2-u02-l04","position":6,"type":"context_choice","skill":"reading","prompt_es":"Leia e responda","payload":{"type":"context_choice","stimulus":{"kind":"reading","id":"ept.stim.b2-u2-leader","document":"post","setting":"Um artigo de revista sobre liderança.","title":"Leaders, not bosses","lines":["What makes a good leader? Many people imagine someone who gives orders and never changes their mind. Research shows the opposite.","The best leaders are flexible. They listen first, and they are willing to compromise when a better idea appears.","They also know how to delegate. Instead of doing everything themselves, they give people responsibility and trust them to do the job.","Finally, they persuade rather than order. When a team understands the reason for a decision, it works harder to make it succeed."]},"question":"Segundo o artigo, por que é melhor convencer em vez de dar ordens?","options":["Porque uma equipe que entende o motivo se esforça mais para que a decisão dê certo","Porque as ordens são ilegais","Porque assim o líder trabalha menos","Porque a equipe sempre tem razão"]},"answer":"Porque uma equipe que entende o motivo se esforça mais para que a decisão dê certo","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"O artigo diz: “When a team understands the reason for a decision, it works harder to make it succeed”.","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":60,"words":[]},{"id":"ept-b2-u02-l04-e07","lesson_id":"ept-b2-u02-l04","position":7,"type":"listen_choice","skill":"listening","prompt_es":"Ouça e escolha o que você ouve","payload":{"type":"listen_choice","audioText":"A good leader listens to the team.","options":["A good leader listens to the team.","A good leader talks to the team.","A good leader listens to the client.","The good leaders listen to the team."]},"answer":"A good leader listens to the team.","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":15,"words":["ept-leader"]},{"id":"ept-b2-u02-l04-e08","lesson_id":"ept-b2-u02-l04","position":8,"type":"context_choice","skill":"reading","prompt_es":"Leia e responda","payload":{"type":"context_choice","stimulus":{"kind":"reading","id":"ept.stim.b2-u2-leader","document":"post","setting":"Um artigo de revista sobre liderança.","title":"Leaders, not bosses","lines":["What makes a good leader? Many people imagine someone who gives orders and never changes their mind. Research shows the opposite.","The best leaders are flexible. They listen first, and they are willing to compromise when a better idea appears.","They also know how to delegate. Instead of doing everything themselves, they give people responsibility and trust them to do the job.","Finally, they persuade rather than order. When a team understands the reason for a decision, it works harder to make it succeed."]},"question":"Segundo o artigo, como são os melhores líderes?","options":["Flexíveis: escutam e cedem se aparece uma ideia melhor","Firmes: nunca mudam de opinião","Exigentes: dão ordens claras","Independentes: fazem tudo sozinhos"]},"answer":"Flexíveis: escutam e cedem se aparece uma ideia melhor","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"O artigo diz: “The best leaders are flexible. They listen first, and they are willing to compromise”.","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":60,"words":[]},{"id":"ept-b2-u02-l04-e09","lesson_id":"ept-b2-u02-l04","position":9,"type":"short_answer","skill":"sentence_building","prompt_es":"Responda em inglês","payload":{"type":"short_answer","question":"How is work at the moment? (você está com trabalho demais)","translation":"Como está o trabalho?"},"answer":"My workload is too heavy.","accepted_answers":["My workload is too heavy at the moment.","I have too much work.","My workload is very heavy."],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":30,"words":["ept-workload"]},{"id":"ept-b2-u02-l04-e10","lesson_id":"ept-b2-u02-l04","position":10,"type":"translate_write","skill":"translation","prompt_es":"Traduza para o inglês","payload":{"type":"translate_write","source":"Na semana passada ela assumiu um projeto novo."},"answer":"She took on a new project last week.","accepted_answers":["Last week she took on a new project.","He took on a new project last week."