:"ept-b2-u03-l01","position":2,"type":"fill_blank","skill":"vocabulary","prompt_es":"Complete a frase","payload":{"type":"fill_blank","sentence":"Working from home is a growing ___.","translation":"Trabalhar de casa é uma tendência que está crescendo.","options":["trend","custom","society","generation"]},"answer":"trend","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":15,"words":["ept-trend"]},{"id":"ept-b2-u03-l01-e03","lesson_id":"ept-b2-u03-l01","position":3,"type":"fill_blank","skill":"vocabulary","prompt_es":"Complete a frase","payload":{"type":"fill_blank","sentence":"In some countries it is a ___ to take off your shoes at home.","translation":"Em alguns países é costume tirar os sapatos em casa.","options":["custom","trend","society","habit"]},"answer":"custom","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"Custom: costume de uma sociedade. Habit: hábito de uma pessoa. E costume, em inglês, é fantasia.","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":15,"words":["ept-custom"]},{"id":"ept-b2-u03-l01-e04","lesson_id":"ept-b2-u03-l01","position":4,"type":"context_choice","skill":"listening","prompt_es":"Ouça e responda","payload":{"type":"context_choice","stimulus":{"kind":"listening","id":"ept.stim.b2-u3-podcast","setting":"Um podcast entrevista uma socióloga sobre as gerações.","speakers":[{"name":"Host","voice":"a"},{"name":"Dr. Reyes","voice":"b"}],"rate":1,"lines":[{"speaker":"Host","text":"People often complain that young people have no respect for old customs. Is that true?"},{"speaker":"Dr. Reyes","text":"Every generation has said that about the next one. It is said that even the ancient Greeks complained about their teenagers."},{"speaker":"Host","text":"So nothing has really changed?"},{"speaker":"Dr. Reyes","text":"Customs change, of course. Fewer people get married in church, for example, and family dinners are less common. But the values behind them haven't disappeared."},{"speaker":"Host","text":"What do you mean?"},{"speaker":"Dr. Reyes","text":"Young people still care about their families. They just show it in different ways: a video call instead of a Sunday lunch."},{"speaker":"Host","text":"And is the gap between generations getting bigger?"},{"speaker":"Dr. Reyes","text":"Honestly, I don't think so. Many people believe that, but my research shows that parents and children agree about most things."}]},"question":"Segundo a socióloga, o que cada geração diz da seguinte?","options":["Que ela não respeita os costumes de antes","Que ela é mais trabalhadora","Que ela vive melhor","Que ela é mais feliz"]},"answer":"Que ela não respeita os costumes de antes","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"O apresentador pergunta se os jovens não respeitam os costumes, e ela responde: “Every generation has said that about the next one”.","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":75,"words":[]},{"id":"ept-b2-u03-l01-e05","lesson_id":"ept-b2-u03-l01","position":5,"type":"context_choice","skill":"listening","prompt_es":"Ouça e responda","payload":{"type":"context_choice","stimulus":{"kind":"listening","id":"ept.stim.b2-u3-podcast","setting":"Um podcast entrevista uma socióloga sobre as gerações.","speakers":[{"name":"Host","voice":"a"},{"name":"Dr. Reyes","voice":"b"}],"rate":1,"lines":[{"speaker":"Host","text":"People often complain that young people have no respect for old customs. Is that true?"},{"speaker":"Dr. Reyes","text":"Every generation has said that about the next one. It is said that even the ancient Greeks complained about their teenagers."},{"speaker":"Host","text":"So nothing has really changed?"},{"speaker":"Dr. Reyes","text":"Customs change, of course. Fewer people get married in church, for example, and family dinners are less common. But the values behind them haven't disappeared."},{"speaker":"Host","text":"What do you mean?"},{"speaker":"Dr. Reyes","text":"Young people still care about their families. They just show it in different ways: a video call instead of a Sunday lunch."},{"speaker":"Host","text":"And is the gap between generations getting bigger?"},{"speaker":"Dr. Reyes","text":"Honestly, I don't think so. Many people believe that, but my research shows that parents and children agree about most things."}]},"question":"O que mudou e o que não mudou, segundo a socióloga?","options":["Mudaram os costumes, mas não os valores","Mudaram os valores, mas não os costumes","Nada mudou","Tudo mudou"]},"answer":"Mudaram os costumes, mas não os valores","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"Ela diz: “Customs change, of course… But the values behind them haven’t disappeared”.","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":75,"words":[]},{"id":"ept-b2-u03-l01-e06","lesson_id":"ept-b2-u03-l01","position":6,"type":"listen_choice","skill":"listening","prompt_es":"Ouça e escolha o que você ouve","payload":{"type":"listen_choice","audioText":"Technology has changed our society.","options":["Technology has changed our society.","Technology will change our society.","Technology has changed our generation.","The internet has changed our society."]},"answer":"Technology has changed our society.","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":15,"words":["ept-society"]},{"id":"ept-b2-u03-l01-e07","lesson_id":"ept-b2-u03-l01","position":7,"type":"order_words","skill":"sentence_building","prompt_es":"Ordene as palavras","payload":{"type":"order_words","tokens":["My","generation","grew","up","with","the","internet"],"translation":"Minha geração cresceu com a internet."},"answer":"My generation grew up with the internet.","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":25,"words":["ept-generation"]},{"id":"ept-b2-u03-l01-e08","lesson_id":"ept-b2-u03-l01","position":8,"type":"short_answer","skill":"sentence_building","prompt_es":"Responda em inglês","payload":{"type":"short_answer","question":"What is a big trend in your country? (trabalhar de casa)","translation":"Qual é uma grande tendência no seu país?"},"answer":"Working from home is a big trend.","accepted_answers":["Working from home.","Working from home is a growing trend.","Working from home is a trend."],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":30,"words":["ept-trend"]},{"id":"ept-b2-u03-l01-e09","lesson_id":"ept-b2-u03-l01","position":9,"type":"translate_write","skill":"translation","prompt_es":"Traduza para o inglês","payload":{"type":"translate_write","source":"A tecnologia mudou a nossa sociedade."},"answer":"Technology has changed our society.","accepted_answers":["Technology changed our society.","Technology's changed our society."],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":30,"words":["ept-society"]},{"id":"ept-b2-u03-l02-e01","lesson_id":"ept-b2-u03-l02","position":1,"type":"match_pairs","skill":"vocabulary","prompt_es":"Una cada palavra ao seu significado","payload":{"type":"match_pairs","pairs":[{"left":"population","right":"população"},{"left":"majority","right":"maioria"},{"left":"minority","right":"minoria"},{"left":"survey","right":"pesquisa"}]},"answer":"","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":30,"words":["ept-population","ept-majority","ept-minority","ept-survey"]},{"id":"ept-b2-u03-l02-e02","lesson_id":"ept-b2-u03-l02","position":2,"type":"fill_blank","skill":"grammar","prompt_es":"Complete a frase","payload":{"type":"fill_blank","sentence":"Prices have ___ a lot this year.","translation":"Os preços aumentaram muito este ano.","options":["risen","rose","rise","rised"]},"answer":"risen","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"Rise é irregular: rise, rose, risen. Com have vem o particípio: have risen.","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":15,"words":["ept-rise"]},{"id":"ept-b2-u03-l02-e03","lesson_id":"ept-b2-u03-l02","position":3,"type":"fill_blank","skill":"vocabulary","prompt_es":"Complete a frase","payload":{"type":"fill_blank","sentence":"The ___ family has fewer than two children.","translation":"A família média tem menos de dois filhos.","options":["average","majority","minority","population"]},"answer":"average","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":15,"words":["ept-average"]},{"id":"ept-b2-u03-l02-e04","lesson_id":"ept-b2-u03-l02","position":4,"type":"context_choice","skill":"reading","prompt_es":"Leia e responda","payload":{"type":"context_choice","stimulus":{"kind":"reading","id":"ept.stim.b2-u3-alone","document":"post","setting":"Um artigo sobre uma pesquisa a respeito das pessoas que moram sozinhas.","title":"A table for one","lines":["Living alone used to be unusual. Today it is one of the biggest trends in our society.","According to a recent survey, one in four homes now has only one person in it. Fifty years ago, the figure was one in ten.","The majority of people who live alone are over sixty, but the number of young people living alone is also rising.","It is often said that living alone makes people lonely. However, the survey suggests the opposite: most people who live alone said they were happy with their lives.","What has declined is the number of large families. In 1970 the average family had four children. Today it has fewer than two."]},"question":"Como mudou o número de lares de uma pessoa só?","options":["Passou de um em cada dez para um em cada quatro","Passou de um em cada quatro para um em cada dez","Não mudou","Caiu pela metade"]},"answer":"Passou de um em cada dez para um em cada quatro","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"O artigo diz: “one in four homes now has only one person in it. Fifty years ago, the figure was one in ten”.","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":60,"words":[]},{"id":"ept-b2-u03-l02-e05","lesson_id":"ept-b2-u03-l02","position":5,"type":"context_choice","skill":"reading","prompt_es":"Leia e responda","payload":{"type":"context_choice","stimulus":{"kind":"reading","id":"ept.stim.b2-u3-alone","document":"post","setting":"Um artigo sobre uma pesquisa a respeito das pessoas que moram sozinhas.","title":"A table for one","lines":["Living alone used to be unusual. Today it is one of the biggest trends in our society.","According to a recent survey, one in four homes now has only one person in it. Fifty years ago, the figure was one in ten.","The majority of people who live alone are over sixty, but the number of young people living alone is also rising.","It is often said that living alone makes people lonely. However, the survey suggests the opposite: most people who live alone said they were happy with their lives.","What has declined is the number of large families. In 1970 the average family had four children. Today it has fewer than two."]},"question":"O que a pesquisa diz sobre a ideia de que morar sozinho deixa a pessoa solitária?","options":["Que a maioria de quem mora sozinho diz ser feliz","Que é verdade","Que só vale para os jovens","Que ela não perguntou isso"]},"answer":"Que a maioria de quem mora sozinho diz ser feliz","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"O artigo diz: “the survey suggests the opposite: most people who live alone said they were happy”.","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":60,"words":[]},{"id":"ept-b2-u03-l02-e06","lesson_id":"ept-b2-u03-l02","position":6,"type":"context_choice","skill":"reading","prompt_es":"Leia e responda","payload":{"type":"context_choice","stimulus":{"kind":"reading","id":"ept.stim.b2-u3-alone","document":"post","setting":"Um artigo sobre uma pesquisa a respeito das pessoas que moram sozinhas.","title":"A table for one","lines":["Living alone used to be unusual. Today it is one of the biggest trends in our society.","According to a recent survey, one in four homes now has only one person in it. Fifty years ago, the figure was one in ten.","The majority of people who live alone are over sixty, but the number of young people living alone is also rising.","It is often said that living alone makes people lonely. However, the survey suggests the opposite: most people who live alone said they were happy with their lives.","What has declined is the number of large families. In 1970 the average family had four children. Today it has fewer than two."]},"question":"O que diminuiu, segundo o artigo?","options":["O número de famílias numerosas","O número de idosos","O número de lares","O número de jovens"]},"answer":"O número de famílias numerosas","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"O artigo diz: “What has declined is the number of large families”.","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":60,"words":[]},{"id":"ept-b2-u03-l02-e07","lesson_id":"ept-b2-u03-l02","position":7,"type":"listen_choice","skill":"listening","prompt_es":"Ouça e escolha o que você ouve","payload":{"type":"listen_choice","audioText":"The population of the city has risen.","options":["The population of the city has risen.","The population of the city has declined.","The population of the country has risen.","The population of the city will rise."]},"answer":"The population of the city has risen.","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":15,"words":["ept-population","ept-rise"]},{"id":"ept-b2-u03-l02-e08","lesson_id":"ept-b2-u03-l02","position":8,"type":"order_words","skill":"sentence_building","prompt_es":"Ordene as palavras","payload":{"type":"order_words","tokens":["Only","a","minority","of","students","live","alone"],"translation":"Só uma minoria dos estudantes mora sozinha."},"answer":"Only a minority of students live alone.","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":25,"words":["ept-minority"]},{"id":"ept-b2-u03-l02-e09","lesson_id":"ept-b2-u03-l02","position":9,"type":"short_answer","skill":"sentence_building","prompt_es":"Responda em inglês","payload":{"type":"short_answer","question":"Has the number of large families risen? (não, diminuiu)","translation":"O número de famílias numerosas aumentou?"},"answer":"No, it has declined.","accepted_answers":["No, it's declined.","No, it declined.","No. It has declined."],"expla