n generations getting bigger?"},{"speaker":"Dr. Reyes","text":"Honestly, I don't think so. Many people believe that, but my research shows that parents and children agree about most things."}]},"question":"Por que a socióloga menciona os gregos antigos?","options":["Para mostrar que a reclamação sobre os jovens é muito antiga","Para falar da história da Grécia","Para dizer que os gregos eram melhores","Para explicar um costume grego"]},"answer":"Para mostrar que a reclamação sobre os jovens é muito antiga","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"Ela diz: “It is said that even the ancient Greeks complained about their teenagers”.","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":75,"words":[]},{"id":"ept-b2-u03-l03-e05","lesson_id":"ept-b2-u03-l03","position":5,"type":"context_choice","skill":"listening","prompt_es":"Ouça e responda","payload":{"type":"context_choice","stimulus":{"kind":"listening","id":"ept.stim.b2-u3-podcast","setting":"Um podcast entrevista uma socióloga sobre as gerações.","speakers":[{"name":"Host","voice":"a"},{"name":"Dr. Reyes","voice":"b"}],"rate":1,"lines":[{"speaker":"Host","text":"People often complain that young people have no respect for old customs. Is that true?"},{"speaker":"Dr. Reyes","text":"Every generation has said that about the next one. It is said that even the ancient Greeks complained about their teenagers."},{"speaker":"Host","text":"So nothing has really changed?"},{"speaker":"Dr. Reyes","text":"Customs change, of course. Fewer people get married in church, for example, and family dinners are less common. But the values behind them haven't disappeared."},{"speaker":"Host","text":"What do you mean?"},{"speaker":"Dr. Reyes","text":"Young people still care about their families. They just show it in different ways: a video call instead of a Sunday lunch."},{"speaker":"Host","text":"And is the gap between generations getting bigger?"},{"speaker":"Dr. Reyes","text":"Honestly, I don't think so. Many people believe that, but my research shows that parents and children agree about most things."}]},"question":"O que a socióloga acha da ideia de que a distância entre as gerações está cada vez maior?","options":["Que muita gente acredita nisso, mas a pesquisa dela não confirma","Que é verdade","Que é uma ideia nova","Que ninguém acredita nisso"]},"answer":"Que muita gente acredita nisso, mas a pesquisa dela não confirma","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"Ela diz: “Many people believe that, but my research shows that parents and children agree about most things”.","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":75,"words":[]},{"id":"ept-b2-u03-l03-e06","lesson_id":"ept-b2-u03-l03","position":6,"type":"context_choice","skill":"reading","prompt_es":"Leia e responda","payload":{"type":"context_choice","stimulus":{"kind":"reading","id":"ept.stim.b2-u3-market","document":"notice","setting":"Um aviso da prefeitura sobre o mercado antigo.","title":"Our market is changing","lines":["The old market is being renovated and will be closed until the end of May.","The roof has already been repaired, and new lights are being installed this month.","The market has been used by local families for more than a hundred years. It is believed to be the oldest building in the neighborhood.","When the work is finished, the market will be used for concerts and festivals. The first festival is expected to take place in June.","Questions can be sent to the community office."]},"question":"O que se acredita sobre o mercado?","options":["Que é o prédio mais antigo do bairro","Que vai fechar para sempre","Que é o maior da cidade","Que foi construído por uma família"]},"answer":"Que é o prédio mais antigo do bairro","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"O aviso diz: “It is believed to be the oldest building in the neighborhood”.","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":60,"words":[]},{"id":"ept-b2-u03-l03-e07","lesson_id":"ept-b2-u03-l03","position":7,"type":"listen_choice","skill":"listening","prompt_es":"Ouça e escolha o que você ouve","payload":{"type":"listen_choice","audioText":"It is said that the house is two hundred years old.","options":["It is said that the house is two hundred years old.","It is said that the house is three hundred years old.","It was said that the house was two hundred years old.","They say that the house is two hundred years old."]},"answer":"It is said that the house is two hundred years old.","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":15,"words":["ept-it-is-said"]},{"id":"ept-b2-u03-l03-e08","lesson_id":"ept-b2-u03-l03","position":8,"type":"order_words","skill":"sentence_building","prompt_es":"Ordene as palavras","payload":{"type":"order_words","tokens":["The","festival","is","expected","to","take","place","in","June"],"translation":"Espera-se que o festival aconteça em junho."},"answer":"The festival is expected to take place in June.","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":25,"words":["ept-be-expected-to","ept-take-place"]},{"id":"ept-b2-u03-l03-e09","lesson_id":"ept-b2-u03-l03","position":9,"type":"short_answer","skill":"sentence_building","prompt_es":"Responda em inglês","payload":{"type":"short_answer","question":"When will the homes be ready? (espera-se que fiquem prontas no ano que vem)","translation":"Quando as moradias vão ficar prontas?"},"answer":"They are expected to be ready next year.","accepted_answers":["They're expected to be ready next year.","They are expected to be finished next year.","Next year, they are expected to be ready."],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":30,"words":["ept-be-expected-to"]},{"id":"ept-b2-u03-l03-e10","lesson_id":"ept-b2-u03-l03","position":10,"type":"translate_write","skill":"translation","prompt_es":"Traduza para o inglês","payload":{"type":"translate_write","source":"Dizem que a casa tem duzentos anos."},"answer":"It is said that the house is two hundred years old.","accepted_answers":["It's said that the house is two hundred years old.","It is said the house is two hundred years old.","The house is said to be two hundred years old."],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":30,"words":["ept-it-is-said"]},{"id":"ept-b2-u03-l04-e01","lesson_id":"ept-b2-u03-l04","position":1,"type":"match_pairs","skill":"vocabulary","prompt_es":"Una cada palavra ao seu significado","payload":{"type":"match_pairs","pairs":[{"left":"housing","right":"moradia"},{"left":"take place","right":"acontecer / ser realizado"},{"left":"is being built","right":"está sendo construído"},{"left":"widespread","right":"generalizado / difundido"}]},"answer":"","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":30,"words":["ept-housing","ept-take-place","ept-being-built","ept-widespread"]},{"id":"ept-b2-u03-l04-e02","lesson_id":"ept-b2-u03-l04","position":2,"type":"fill_blank","skill":"grammar","prompt_es":"Complete a frase","payload":{"type":"fill_blank","sentence":"A new school is ___ built near my house.","translation":"Uma escola nova está sendo construída perto da minha casa.","options":["being","been","be","was"]},"answer":"being","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"Passiva contínua: is / are + being + particípio.","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":15,"words":["ept-being-built"]},{"id":"ept-b2-u03-l04-e03","lesson_id":"ept-b2-u03-l04","position":3,"type":"fill_blank","skill":"grammar","prompt_es":"Complete a frase","payload":{"type":"fill_blank","sentence":"The roof has already ___ repaired.","translation":"O telhado já foi consertado.","options":["been","being","be","was"]},"answer":"been","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"Passiva no present perfect: has / have + been + particípio.","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":15,"words":["ept-being-built"]},{"id":"ept-b2-u03-l04-e04","lesson_id":"ept-b2-u03-l04","position":4,"type":"fill_blank","skill":"vocabulary","prompt_es":"Complete a frase","payload":{"type":"fill_blank","sentence":"The festival will take ___ in the old market.","translation":"O festival vai ser realizado no mercado antigo.","options":["place","part","time","care"]},"answer":"place","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":15,"words":["ept-take-place"]},{"id":"ept-b2-u03-l04-e05","lesson_id":"ept-b2-u03-l04","position":5,"type":"context_choice","skill":"listening","prompt_es":"Ouça e responda","payload":{"type":"context_choice","stimulus":{"kind":"listening","id":"ept.stim.b2-u3-radio","setting":"Uma reportagem de rádio sobre o último censo de uma cidade.","speakers":[{"name":"Presenter","voice":"a"},{"name":"Anna","voice":"b"}],"rate":1,"lines":[{"speaker":"Presenter","text":"Good morning. The results of the new census have just been published. Anna, what do they tell us?"},{"speaker":"Anna","text":"The population of the city has risen by ten percent in five years, mainly because of young people from other regions."},{"speaker":"Presenter","text":"And where are they living?"},{"speaker":"Anna","text":"That's the problem. Housing is very expensive, so the average young person shares a flat until the age of thirty."},{"speaker":"Presenter","text":"Is anything being done about it?"},{"speaker":"Anna","text":"Two thousand new homes are being built near the river, and more are expected to be ready next year."},{"speaker":"Presenter","text":"Thank you, Anna. In other news, the summer festival will take place in the old market this year."}]},"question":"Por que os jovens dividem apartamento até os trinta, segundo a reportagem?","options":["Porque a moradia é muito cara","Porque não conseguem emprego","Porque preferem morar com amigos","Porque estudam até os trinta"]},"answer":"Porque a moradia é muito cara","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"Anna diz: “Housing is very expensive, so the average young person shares a flat until the age of thirty”.","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":75,"words":[]},{"id":"ept-b2-u03-l04-e06","lesson_id":"ept-b2-u03-l04","position":6,