vens.","options":["be","being","been","to be"]},"answer":"be","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"Passiva com modal: should / can / will + be + particípio.","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":15,"words":["ept-housing"]},{"id":"ept-b2-u03-l05-e03","lesson_id":"ept-b2-u03-l05","position":3,"type":"fill_blank","skill":"grammar","prompt_es":"Complete a frase","payload":{"type":"fill_blank","sentence":"Many languages can be ___ in the market.","translation":"No mercado dá para ouvir muitos idiomas.","options":["heard","hear","hearing","hears"]},"answer":"heard","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":15,"words":["ept-diversity"]},{"id":"ept-b2-u03-l05-e04","lesson_id":"ept-b2-u03-l05","position":4,"type":"context_choice","skill":"listening","prompt_es":"Ouça e responda","payload":{"type":"context_choice","stimulus":{"kind":"listening","id":"ept.stim.b2-u3-podcast","setting":"Um podcast entrevista uma socióloga sobre as gerações.","speakers":[{"name":"Host","voice":"a"},{"name":"Dr. Reyes","voice":"b"}],"rate":1,"lines":[{"speaker":"Host","text":"People often complain that young people have no respect for old customs. Is that true?"},{"speaker":"Dr. Reyes","text":"Every generation has said that about the next one. It is said that even the ancient Greeks complained about their teenagers."},{"speaker":"Host","text":"So nothing has really changed?"},{"speaker":"Dr. Reyes","text":"Customs change, of course. Fewer people get married in church, for example, and family dinners are less common. But the values behind them haven't disappeared."},{"speaker":"Host","text":"What do you mean?"},{"speaker":"Dr. Reyes","text":"Young people still care about their families. They just show it in different ways: a video call instead of a Sunday lunch."},{"speaker":"Host","text":"And is the gap between generations getting bigger?"},{"speaker":"Dr. Reyes","text":"Honestly, I don't think so. Many people believe that, but my research shows that parents and children agree about most things."}]},"question":"Como os jovens mostram hoje que se importam com a família, segundo a socióloga?","options":["De outro jeito, por exemplo com uma chamada de vídeo em vez de um almoço","Eles não mostram mais","Morando com os pais","Indo à igreja"]},"answer":"De outro jeito, por exemplo com uma chamada de vídeo em vez de um almoço","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"Ela diz: “They just show it in different ways: a video call instead of a Sunday lunch”.","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":75,"words":[]},{"id":"ept-b2-u03-l05-e05","lesson_id":"ept-b2-u03-l05","position":5,"type":"context_choice","skill":"reading","prompt_es":"Leia e responda","payload":{"type":"context_choice","stimulus":{"kind":"reading","id":"ept.stim.b2-u3-market","document":"notice","setting":"Um aviso da prefeitura sobre o mercado antigo.","title":"Our market is changing","lines":["The old market is being renovated and will be closed until the end of May.","The roof has already been repaired, and new lights are being installed this month.","The market has been used by local families for more than a hundred years. It is believed to be the oldest building in the neighborhood.","When the work is finished, the market will be used for concerts and festivals. The first festival is expected to take place in June.","Questions can be sent to the community office."]},"question":"Para que o mercado vai ser usado quando as obras terminarem?","options":["Para shows e festivais","Para moradias","Para escritórios","Como escola"]},"answer":"Para shows e festivais","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"O aviso diz: “the market will be used for concerts and festivals”.","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":60,"words":[]},{"id":"ept-b2-u03-l05-e06","lesson_id":"ept-b2-u03-l05","position":6,"type":"listen_choice","skill":"listening","prompt_es":"Ouça e escolha o que você ouve","payload":{"type":"listen_choice","audioText":"The diversity of the city is its best quality.