on":"O telefone, que foi inventado em 1876, mudou o mundo.","options":["which","that","whose","who"]},"answer":"which","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"Numa explicativa (entre vírgulas) não se usa that: which para coisas, who para pessoas.","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":15,"words":["ept-invention"]},{"id":"ept-b2-u04-l03-e02","lesson_id":"ept-b2-u04-l03","position":2,"type":"fill_blank","skill":"grammar","prompt_es":"Complete a frase","payload":{"type":"fill_blank","sentence":"One of our experiments failed, ___ was very frustrating.","translation":"Um dos nossos experimentos falhou, o que foi muito frustrante.","options":["which","that","what","who"]},"answer":"which","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"Which retoma a oração anterior inteira (o que).","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":15,"words":["ept-experiment"]},{"id":"ept-b2-u04-l03-e03","lesson_id":"ept-b2-u04-l03","position":3,"type":"fill_blank","skill":"grammar","prompt_es":"Complete a frase","payload":{"type":"fill_blank","sentence":"I have many books, most of ___ I have never read.","translation":"Tenho muitos livros, a maioria dos quais eu nunca li.","options":["which","them","that","whose"]},"answer":"which","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"Most of which: depois de uma vírgula, não se repete them.","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":15,"words":["ept-most-of-which"]},{"id":"ept-b2-u04-l03-e04","lesson_id":"ept-b2-u04-l03","position":4,"type":"context_choice","skill":"listening","prompt_es":"Ouça e responda","payload":{"type":"context_choice","stimulus":{"kind":"listening","id":"ept.stim.b2-u4-interview","setting":"Uma entrevista de rádio com uma cientista que inventou um filtro de água.","speakers":[{"name":"Host","voice":"a"},{"name":"Mei","voice":"b"}],"rate":1,"lines":[{"speaker":"Host","text":"My guest today is Dr. Mei Lin, whose team has come up with a new way to clean water. Welcome."},{"speaker":"Mei","text":"Thank you. Our filter, which costs less than five dollars, uses only sunlight to clean dirty water."},{"speaker":"Host","text":"That sounds like a real breakthrough. How did you get the idea?"},{"speaker":"Mei","text":"By accident, actually. One of our experiments failed, which was very frustrating at the time. But the results showed something we didn't expect."},{"speaker":"Host","text":"And is there evidence that it works outside the lab?"},{"speaker":"Mei","text":"Yes. We have tested it in forty villages, most of which have no clean water. The data are very clear."},{"speaker":"Host","text":"What is the next step?"},{"speaker":"Mei","text":"We want to make it in large numbers. The invention is useless if the people who need it can't get it."}]},"question":"Como é a maioria dos vilarejos onde testaram o filtro?","options":["Não têm água limpa","Ficam perto do laboratório","Têm muito sol","São muito grandes"]},"answer":"Não têm água limpa","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"Mei diz: “We have tested it in forty villages, most of which have no clean water”.","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":75,"words":[]},{"id":"ept-b2-u04-l03-e05","lesson_id":"ept-b2-u04-l03","position":5,"type":"context_choice","skill":"reading","prompt_es":"Leia e responda","payload":{"type":"context_choice","stimulus":{"kind":"reading","id":"ept.stim.b2-u4-museum","document":"notice","setting":"Painéis de uma sala de um museu de ciência.","title":"Science Museum","lines":["Room 3: Ideas that changed the world","The telephone, which was invented in 1876, allowed people to talk across long distances for the first time.","Marie Curie, whose discoveries changed medicine, was the first person to win two Nobel Prizes.","The World Wide Web was created by Tim Berners-Lee, a scientist for whom sharing information was more important than money. He never asked for payment for his invention.","Which of these innovations do you use every day?"]},"question":"Por que o painel lembra Marie Curie?","options":["Suas descobertas mudaram a medicina e ela ganhou dois prêmios Nobel","Inventou o telefone","Criou a World Wide Web","Foi a primeira médica"]},"answer":"Suas descobertas mudaram a medicina e ela ganhou dois prêmios Nobel","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"O painel diz: “Marie Curie, whose discoveries changed medicine, was the first person to win two Nobel Prizes”.","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":60,"words":[]},{"id":"ept-b2-u04-l03-e06","lesson_id":"ept-b2-u04-l03","position":6,"type":"listen_choice","skill":"listening","prompt_es":"Ouça e escolha o que você ouve","payload":{"type":"listen_choice","audioText":"I have many books, most of which I have never read.","options":["I have many books, most of which I have never read.","I have many books, all of which I have read.","I have some books, most of which I have never read.","I have many books, which I have never read."]},"answer":"I have many books, most of which I have never read.","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":15,"words":["ept-most-of-which"]},{"id":"ept-b2-u04-l03-e07","lesson_id":"ept-b2-u04-l03","position":7,"type":"order_words","skill":"sentence_building","prompt_es":"Ordene as palavras","payload":{"type":"order_words","tokens":["My","brother","who","lives","in","London","is","a","scientist"],"translation":"Meu irmão que mora em Londres é cientista."},"answer":"My brother who lives in London is a scientist.","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":25,"words":["ept-scientist"]},{"id":"ept-b2-u04-l03-e08","lesson_id":"ept-b2-u04-l03","position":8,"type":"short_answer","skill":"sentence_building","prompt_es":"Responda em inglês","payload":{"type":"short_answer","question":"How did the experiment go? (falhou, o que foi frustrante)","translation":"Como foi o experimento?"},"answer":"It failed, which was frustrating.","accepted_answers":["It failed, which was very frustrating.","The experiment failed, which was frustrating.","It failed which was frustrating."],"expl