conds":15,"words":["ept-empathy"]},{"id":"ept-b2-u06-l05-e03","lesson_id":"ept-b2-u06-l05","position":3,"type":"fill_blank","skill":"vocabulary","prompt_es":"Complete a frase","payload":{"type":"fill_blank","sentence":"Learning a language gave me more ___.","translation":"Aprender um idioma me deu mais autoconfiança.","options":["self-confidence","empathy","mood","evidence"]},"answer":"self-confidence","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":15,"words":["ept-self-confidence"]},{"id":"ept-b2-u06-l05-e04","lesson_id":"ept-b2-u06-l05","position":4,"type":"context_choice","skill":"listening","prompt_es":"Ouça e responda","payload":{"type":"context_choice","stimulus":{"kind":"listening","id":"ept.stim.b2-u6-podcast","setting":"Um podcast sobre psicologia entrevista um psicólogo.","speakers":[{"name":"Host","voice":"a"},{"name":"Dr. Moss","voice":"b"}],"rate":1,"lines":[{"speaker":"Host","text":"Today we are talking about empathy. What exactly is it?"},{"speaker":"Dr. Moss","text":"It is the ability to understand how another person feels, to put yourself in their shoes. It's not the same as agreeing with them."},{"speaker":"Host","text":"Can empathy be learned?"},{"speaker":"Dr. Moss","text":"Yes. The first step is to listen without judging. Most of us listen only to answer."},{"speaker":"Host","text":"Some listeners say their mood changes very quickly. Is that normal?"},{"speaker":"Dr. Moss","text":"Everybody has good and bad days. But if you are often in a bad mood, it might be stress, or a lack of sleep."},{"speaker":"Host","text":"And what about self-confidence?"},{"speaker":"Dr. Moss","text":"People with low self-confidence tend to think that others are judging them. Usually, others are too busy thinking about themselves!"}]},"question":"Segundo o psicólogo, empatia é o mesmo que concordar?","options":["Não: é entender como o outro se sente, mesmo sem concordar","Sim, é a mesma coisa","Sim, mas só com amigos","Não: é dar conselhos"]},"answer":"Não: é entender como o outro se sente, mesmo sem concordar","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"Ele diz: “It is the ability to understand how another person feels… It’s not the same as agreeing with them”.","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":75,"words":[]},{"id":"ept-b2-u06-l05-e05","lesson_id":"ept-b2-u06-l05","position":5,"type":"context_choice","skill":"listening","prompt_es":"Ouça e responda","payload":{"type":"context_choice","stimulus":{"kind":"listening","id":"ept.stim.b2-u6-podcast","setting":"Um podcast sobre psicologia entrevista um psicólogo.","speakers":[{"name":"Host","voice":"a"},{"name":"Dr. Moss","voice":"b"}],"rate":1,"lines":[{"speaker":"Host","text":"Today we are talking about empathy. What exactly is it?"},{"speaker":"Dr. Moss","text":"It is the ability to understand how another person feels, to put yourself in their shoes. It's not the same as agreeing with them."},{"speaker":"Host","text":"Can empathy be learned?"},{"speaker":"Dr. Moss","text":"Yes. The first step is to listen without judging. Most of us listen only to answer."},{"speaker":"Host","text":"Some listeners say their mood changes very quickly. Is that normal?"},{"speaker":"Dr. Moss","text":"Everybody has good and bad days. But if you are often in a bad mood, it might be stress, or a lack of sleep."},{"speaker":"Host","text":"And what about self-confidence?"},{"speaker":"Dr. Moss","text":"People with low self-confidence tend to think that others are judging them. Usually, others are too busy thinking about themselves!"}]},"question":"O que pode estar por trás de ficar de mau humor com frequência?","options":["Estresse ou falta de sono","Uma alimentação ruim","Trabalho em equipe demais","O clima"]},"answer":"Estresse ou falta de sono","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"Ele diz: “if you are often in a bad mood, it might be stress, or a lack of sleep”.","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":75,"words":[]},{"id":"ept-b2-u06-l05-e06","lesson_id":"ept-b2-u06-l05","position":6,"type":"context_choice","skill":"listening","prompt_es":"Ouça e responda","payload":{"type":"context_choice","stimulus":{"kind":"listening","id":"ept.stim.b2-u6-podcast","setting":"Um podcast sobre psicologia entrevista um psicólogo.","speakers":[{"name":"Host","voice":"a"},{"name":"Dr. Moss","voice":"b"}],"rate":1,"lines":[{"speaker":"Host","text":"Today we are talking about empathy. What exactly is it?"},{"speaker":"Dr. Moss","text":"It is the ability to understand how another person feels, to put yourself in their shoes. It's not the same as agreeing with them."},{"speaker":"Host","text":"Can empathy be learned?"},{"speaker":"Dr. Moss","text":"Yes. The first step is to listen without judging. Most of us listen only to answer."},{"speaker":"Host","text":"Some listeners say their mood changes very quickly. Is that normal?"},{"speaker":"Dr. Moss","text":"Everybody has good and bad days. But if you are often in a bad mood, it might be stress, or a lack of sleep."},{"speaker":"Host","text":"And what about self-confidence?"},{"speaker":"Dr. Moss","text":"People with low self-confidence tend to think that others are judging them. Usually, others are too busy thinking about themselves!"}]},"question":"O que ele diz, com humor, sobre as pessoas com pouca autoconfiança?","options":["Acham que os outros as julgam, mas os outros estão pensando em si mesmos","Que nunca mudam","Que têm razão","Que deveriam falar mais"]},"answer":"Acham que os outros as julgam, mas os outros estão pensando em si mesmos","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"Ele diz: “People with low self-confidence tend to think that others are judging them. Usually, others are too busy thinking about themselves!”.","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":75,"words":[]},{"id":"ept-b2-u06-l05-e07","lesson_id":"ept-b2-u06-l05","position":7,"type":"listen_choice","skill":"listening","prompt_es":"Ouça e escolha o que você ouve","payload":{"type":"listen_choice","audioText":"Empathy means understanding how others feel.","options":["Empathy means understanding how others feel.","Empathy means understanding how you feel.","Empathy means telling others how you feel.","Empathy means knowing what others think."]},"answer":"Empathy means understanding how others feel.","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":15,"words":["ept-empathy"]},{"id":"ept-b2-u06-l05-e08","lesson_id":"ept-b2-u06-l05","position":8,"type":"order_words","skill":"sentence_building","prompt_es":"Ordene as palavras","payload":{"type":"order_words","tokens":["He","is","too","stubborn","to","say","sorry"],"translation":"Ele é teimoso demais para pedir desculpas."},"answer":"He is too stubborn to say sorry.","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":25,"words":["ept-stubborn"]},{"id":"ept-b2-u06-l05-e09","lesson_id":"ept-b2-u06-l05","position":9,"type":"short_answer","skill":"sentence_building","prompt_es":"Responda em inglês","payload":{"type":"short_answer","question":"How has learning English helped you? (te deu mais autoconfiança)","translation":"Em que aprender inglês te ajudou?"},"answer":"It has given me more self-confidence.","accepted_answers":["It's given me more self-confidence.","It gave me more self-confidence.","It has given me more confidence."],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":30,"words":["ept-self-confidence"]},{"id":"ept-b2-u06-l05-e10","lesson_id":"ept-b2-u06-l05","position":10,"type":"translate_write","skill":"translation","prompt_es":"Traduza para o inglês","payload":{"type":"translate_write","source":"Ele é teimoso demais para pedir desculpas."},"answer":"He is too stubborn to say sorry.","accepted_answers":["He's too stubborn to say sorry.","He is too stubborn to apologize.","He's too stubborn to apologize.","She is too stubborn to say sorry."],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":30,"words":["ept-stubborn"]},{"id":"ept-b2-u06-listen-e01","lesson_id":"ept-