"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":15,"words":["ept-outweigh"]},{"id":"ept-b2-u10-l05-e03","lesson_id":"ept-b2-u10-l05","position":3,"type":"fill_blank","skill":"vocabulary","prompt_es":"Complete a frase","payload":{"type":"fill_blank","sentence":"To sum ___, I think the plan is a good idea.","translation":"Em resumo, acho que o plano é uma boa ideia.","options":["up","out","on","off"]},"answer":"up","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":15,"words":["ept-to-sum-up"]},{"id":"ept-b2-u10-l05-e04","lesson_id":"ept-b2-u10-l05","position":4,"type":"context_choice","skill":"reading","prompt_es":"Leia e responda","payload":{"type":"context_choice","stimulus":{"kind":"reading","id":"ept.stim.b2-u10-free-uni","document":"post","setting":"Um artigo de opinião sobre a universidade gratuita.","title":"Education is an investment, not a cost","lines":["Should university be free? I believe it should.","First, education benefits everyone, not only the student. Educated citizens earn more, pay more taxes and are healthier. Furthermore, free education gives poor students the same chances as rich ones.","Admittedly, free universities cost the government a lot of money, and some people argue that students should pay for their own future. Nevertheless, the long-term benefits outweigh the costs.","It is not the cost of education that should worry us, but the cost of ignorance.","To sum up, free university is not a gift. It is an investment in all of us."]},"question":"Com que ideia a autora fecha o texto?","options":["Que a universidade gratuita é um investimento em todos, não um presente","Que a universidade deveria ser mais barata","Que os alunos devem pagar","Que o governo gasta mal"]},"answer":"Que a universidade gratuita é um investimento em todos, não um presente","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"O artigo termina: “To sum up, free university is not a gift. It is an investment in all of us”.","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":60,"words":[]},{"id":"ept-b2-u10-l05-e05","lesson_id":"ept-b2-u10-l05","position":5,"type":"context_choice","skill":"reading","prompt_es":"Leia e responda","payload":{"type":"context_choice","stimulus":{"kind":"reading","id":"ept.stim.b2-u10-free-uni","document":"post","setting":"Um artigo de opinião sobre a universidade gratuita.","title":"Education is an investment, not a cost","lines":["Should university be free? I believe it should.","First, education benefits everyone, not only the student. Educated citizens earn more, pay more taxes and are healthier. Furthermore, free education gives poor students the same chances as rich ones.","Admittedly, free universities cost the government a lot of money, and some people argue that students should pay for their own future. Nevertheless, the long-term benefits outweigh the costs.","It is not the cost of education that should worry us, but the cost of ignorance.","To sum up, free university is not a gift. It is an investment in all of us."]},"question":"O que a frase “It is not the cost of education that should worry us, but the cost of ignorance” enfatiza?","options":["Que o que sai caro de verdade é não educar as pessoas","Que a educação é muito cara","Que a ignorância não tem custo","Que o governo deveria gastar menos"]},"answer":"Que o que sai caro de verdade é não educar as pessoas","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"Com It is… that…, a autora põe o foco em “the cost of ignorance”: o preocupante não é pagar pela educação, e sim a falta dela.","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":60,"words":[]},{"id":"ept-b2-u10-l05-e06","lesson_id":"ept-b2-u10-l05","position":6,"type":"context_choice","skill":"listening","prompt_es":"Ouça e responda","payload":{"type":"context_choice","stimulus":{"kind":"listening","id":"ept.stim.b2-u10-four-days","setting":"Uns colegas discutem a proposta de trabalhar quatro dias por semana.","speakers":[{"name":"Olivia","voice":"a"},{"name":"Ken","voice":"b"}],"rate":1,"lines":[{"speaker":"Olivia","text":"So, the four-day week. What worries me is the customers. Who answers the phone on Fridays?"},{"speaker":"Ken","text":"We'd take turns. The reason why other companies have done it is that people work better when they're rested."},{"speaker":"Olivia","text":"That may be true for some jobs. But we need to take into account that our clients expect us every day."},{"speaker":"Ken","text":"That's a valid point. So let's try it for three months and measure the results."},{"speaker":"Olivia","text":"OK, I find that convincing. All things considered, a trial is a good compromise."}]},"question":"Como termina a discussão?","options":["A Olivia se convence: testar por três meses é um bom meio-termo","Eles não chegam a um acordo","O Ken retira a proposta","Decidem perguntar ao chefe"]},"answer":"A Olivia se convence: testar por três meses é um bom meio-termo","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"A Olivia diz: “OK, I find that convincing. All things considered, a trial is a good compromise”.","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":75,"words":[]},{"id":"ept-b2-u10-l05-e07","lesson_id":"ept-b2-u10-l05","position":7,"type":"listen_choice","skill":"listening","prompt_es":"Ouça e escolha o que você ouve","payload":{"type":"listen_choice","audioText":"All things considered, it was a good year.","options":["All things considered, it was a good year.","All things considered, it was a bad year.","All things considered, it will be a good year.","All in all, it was a good year."]},"answer":"All things considered, it was a good year.","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":15,"words":["ept-all-things-considered"]},{"id":"ept-b2-u10-l05-e08","lesson_id":"ept-b2-u10-l05","position":8,"type":"short_answer","skill":"sentence_building","prompt_es":"Responda em inglês","payload":{"type":"short_answer","question":"So, should we buy the house? (em resumo, você acha que sim)","translation":"Então, a gente compra a casa?"},"answer":"To sum up, I th