akers":[{"name":"Olivia","voice":"a"},{"name":"Ken","voice":"b"}],"rate":1,"lines":[{"speaker":"Olivia","text":"So, the four-day week. What worries me is the customers. Who answers the phone on Fridays?"},{"speaker":"Ken","text":"We'd take turns. The reason why other companies have done it is that people work better when they're rested."},{"speaker":"Olivia","text":"That may be true for some jobs. But we need to take into account that our clients expect us every day."},{"speaker":"Ken","text":"That's a valid point. So let's try it for three months and measure the results."},{"speaker":"Olivia","text":"OK, I find that convincing. All things considered, a trial is a good compromise."}]},"question":"Segundo o Ken, por que outras empresas adotaram a semana de quatro dias?","options":["Porque as pessoas trabalham melhor quando estão descansadas","Porque economizam dinheiro","Porque os clientes pediram","Porque é a lei"]},"answer":"Porque as pessoas trabalham melhor quando estão descansadas","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"O Ken diz: “The reason why other companies have done it is that people work better when they’re rested”.","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":75,"grading_spec":{"mode":"exact_option","mode_version":1},"generator":null,"generator_version":null},{"item_id":"ept.ex.anr39dorb79q9g","content_hash":"v1:2aec10c45faf3eab1a7f07976015e81f018c588991f8a75163ff5a9d555f0ed5","prompt_es":"Ouça e responda","payload":{"type":"context_choice","stimulus":{"kind":"listening","id":"ept.stim.b2-u10-school-debate","setting":"Um debate em uma escola: os celulares devem ser proibidos na sala de aula?","speakers":[{"name":"Moderator","voice":"a"},{"name":"Lucas","voice":"b"},{"name":"Hannah","voice":"a"}],"rate":1,"lines":[{"speaker":"Moderator","text":"Today's debate: should phones be banned in schools? Lucas, you're first."},{"speaker":"Lucas","text":"Yes, they should. Phones distract students. Moreover, they make bullying easier, because it continues after school. As a result, many students feel anxious all day."},{"speaker":"Moderator","text":"Hannah, your answer?"},{"speaker":"Hannah","text":"Admittedly, phones can be a distraction. Nevertheless, banning them is not the answer. On the contrary, schools should teach students how to use them responsibly."},{"speaker":"Lucas","text":"But that's an assumption. Where is the evidence that teaching works better?"},{"speaker":"Hannah","text":"Fair question. What I'm saying is that a ban doesn't teach anything. In other words, students will just use their phones more at home."}]},"question":"O que a Hannah esclarece com “In other words…”?","options":["Que, com a proibição, os alunos só vão usar mais o celular em casa","Que os celulares são perigosos","Que ela concorda com o Lucas","Que ela não tem provas"]},"answer":"Que, com a proibição, os alunos só vão usar mais o celular em casa","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"A Hannah diz: “a ban doesn’t teach anything. In other words, students will just use their phones more at home”.","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":75,"grading_spec":{"mode":"exact_option","mode_version":1},"generator":null,"generator_version":null},{"item_id":"ept.ex.fz0gkpkc61b29t","content_hash":"v1:fbbe3f950d31e960c50127701ff94168ed43429e67c2061ce40c03dbea1f2f9e","prompt_es":"Ouça e escolha o que você ouve","payload":{"type":"listen_choice","audioText":"What matters is that you tried.","options":["What matters is that you tried.","What matters is that you won.","It doesn't matter that you tried.","What matters is that we tried."]},"answer":"What matters is that you tried.","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":15,"grading_spec":{"mode":"exact_option","mode_version":1},"generator":null,"generator_version":null},{"item_id":"ept.ex.si8zd4c7j1kpei","content_hash":"v1:e69a9270092e6ea71eb7966a908ac297e4b209952811447eb0ddba49f2d8f4c2","prompt_es":"Ordene as palavras","payload":{"type":"order_words","tokens":["What","worries"